// Generated by Qleany v1.9.0 from feature_use_case.tera
// Custom implementation (hand-maintained — do NOT blanket-regenerate): one read-only pass
// over a container's subtree, measuring what the Analysis view shows.
//
// **This writes nothing.** Not the entities it reads, not a dirty flag, not an undo entry:
// `undoable: false`, `read_only: true`, and a `QueryUnitOfWork`. Measuring a manuscript must
// never modify it — `analysis_writes_no_entities` guards that.
//
// Modelled on `scan_mentions_uc`: same `gather`, same `TreeReader` impl, same long-operation
// shape. The measurements themselves live in `skribisto_model::analysis`, store-free and
// unit-tested; everything here is plumbing — resolve the scope, extract plain text once per
// scene, feed the measures, shape the result.
//
// Two scope decisions worth keeping:
//
// * The subtree walk is `compile::row_indices`, **not** `compile::resolve_scope`. The latter
//   is the *export* scope and silently drops `is_exportable == false` rows via `push_swept`.
//   A writer asking "analyse what I wrote" means everything they wrote, including the parts
//   they have chosen not to print.
// * Prose is read once per scene into plain text and reused by every measure. Re-parsing the
//   Djot per metric would multiply the only genuinely expensive step in the pass.
